.TH SONDC 1 "2026-07" "Sond" "Sond Compiler Manual"
.SH NAME
sondc \- compile a Sond source file to a native x86-64 program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sondc
.I input.snd
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.RB [ \-\-freestanding " | " \-\-uefi " | " \-\-shared ]
.RB [ \-\-emit\-header ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sondc
compiles a single Sond source file to a native Linux/amd64 artifact. Before
emitting any code it runs the oracle: every function contract
.RB ( requires / ensures )
is proven at compile time, and a contract the prover cannot verify is a compile
error \(em the program is rejected, not run. Divide\-by\-zero is likewise a compile
error unless the divisor is proven non\-zero.
.PP
.RB "\(bu " include " \fB\(dq...\(dq\fR"
directives are resolved (recursively, deduplicated) so a multi\-file program \(em a
reusable library plus the code that uses it \(em compiles as one unit.
.PP
Successful compiles are cached under
.IR ~/.cache/sond/build ,
keyed on the resolved source, the target, and a fingerprint of the compiler.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Write the artifact to
.IR output
(default: the input's base name).
.TP
.B \-\-freestanding
Link a static, libc\-free binary with its own
.B _start
that exits via a raw syscall \(em the shape of an initramfs
.IR /init .
.TP
.B \-\-uefi
Emit a UEFI application (PE32+/EFI, Microsoft x64 ABI) that firmware loads and runs
on bare hardware. Linked with a PE toolchain as
.IR BOOTX64.EFI .
.TP
.B \-\-shared
Emit a C\-ABI shared object
.RI ( .so ),
position\-independent and libc\-free, with each
.B pub fn
exported in the dynamic symbol table \(em importable from C/C++/Go/Rust/Python.
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-header
Print the module's public interface \(em the
.B pub
declarations with their contracts, bodies stripped \(em and exit.
.SH DEFAULT TARGET
With no target flag, the output is a hosted executable linked with the C runtime;
the entry function's value becomes the process exit code.
.SH INCLUDE RESOLUTION
An
.B include
path is resolved in order: relative to the including file, then a
.I lib/
root found by walking up the tree, then the system library
.IR ~/.local/lib/sond/ .
So an external program writes
.B include \(dqany/crypto/cipher/chacha20.snd\(dq
and it resolves from the installed standard library.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/sondc
The compiler binary (installed by
.IR tools/install.sh ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/lib/sond/
The standard library (a copy of the repository's
.IR lib/ ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/include/sond/
Generated header interfaces.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/sond/build/
Compilation cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success; non\-zero on a parse error, a contract violation, or a failed link.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sond (1),
and the language reference
.IR ~/.local/share/sond/Sond.md .
